  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s beast phantoms are ordinary wild beasts, while a dragon-elephant phantom carries a trace of dragon bloodline and is treated as a mutated beast.",
      "chapters": [
        317
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Beasts have mutated beasts the way humans have mutated humans: Biao among tigers, lycan among wolves, and mastiff among dogs mark that class on the beast side.",
      "chapters": [
        356
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kunlun bull is a mutated beast ranked with Biao, dragon-elephant, thunder boar, and rock crocodile. Fang Yuan can exert kunlun bull strength as a solid phantom strike.",
      "chapters": [
        368
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-examples",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In King Quan Inheritance, lion mastiffs are mutated beasts with much more battle prowess than the five great mountain dogs, and they are called King Quan’s trump cards. Two dog emperors are ancient mutated beasts more powerful than common mutated beasts; each can match a rank five Gu Master and must be subdued.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ancient-mutated-beasts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
